Package: harmorust
Title: 'Rust' Native Kernels for 'Harmony' Single-Cell Integration
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person(
    given = "Nebil",
    family = "Ibrahim",
    email = "nebil.b.ibrahim@gmail.com",
    role = c("aut", "cre")
    )
Description: 'Rust' reimplementation of the 'Harmony' integration loop
    (soft k-means, diversity penalty, mixture-of-experts ridge) with the
    same RunHarmony() signature used by the immunogenomics 'Harmony' R
    package. Designed to sit next to 'seurust': 'Seurat'/'seurust' produce the
    PCA embedding, 'harmorust' corrects it. Installing from source builds the
    'harmorust' CLI with Cargo and places it in the package 'bin' directory.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
URL: https://github.com/NebilI/harmony-rs,
    https://NebilI.r-universe.dev/harmorust
BugReports: https://github.com/NebilI/harmony-rs/issues
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.2)
Imports: jsonlite, stats
Suggests: Seurat (>= 4.1.1), SingleCellExperiment, ggplot2, seurust, testthat (>= 3.0.0)
SystemRequirements: Cargo (Rust's package manager), rustc (>= 1.89)
Config/testthat/edition: 3
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
RoxygenNote: 7.3.2
